@{ ViewData["Title"] = "About"; }
<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9">
        <h1 class="h2">About SkillBridge</h1>
        <p class="lead">A web-based skill marketplace and job/task recruitment management system.</p>
        <p>SkillBridge connects <strong>Employers</strong> who need work completed with skilled <strong>Hunters</strong> who can complete it.
           The platform tracks every step: job posting, applications and bids, applicant comparison, Hunter selection,
           work submission and revision, completion, ratings and payment status.</p>

        <div class="card mb-3"><div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h5">Three concepts kept separate</h2>
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><span class="badge sb-difficulty">Job difficulty</span> — a 1-star, 2-star or 3-star category describing how complex the <em>work</em> is.</li>
                <li><span class="badge sb-skill-level">Skill level</span> — a Hunter's <em>self-reported</em> proficiency (Beginner → Expert) in one particular skill.</li>
                <li><span class="sb-stars"><i class="bi bi-star-fill"></i></span> <strong>Performance rating</strong> — 1–5 stars left only by the other party of a <em>completed</em> assignment.</li>
            </ul>
        </div></div>

        <div class="card mb-3 sb-simulated"><div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h5"><i class="bi bi-cash-coin"></i> Payments are simulated</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">SkillBridge keeps a payment <strong>ledger</strong> (Pending → Awaiting approval → Approved → Paid, plus Failed/Cancelled/Refunded).
            It does not integrate a payment gateway, does not store card details and does not transfer real money.
            "Paid" means the Employer recorded that they paid the Hunter outside the platform.</p>
        </div></div>

        <div class="card"><div class="card-body">
            <h2 class="h5">Project team</h2>
